  "texture_method": "New opaque source images only. Non-grass materials retain bilinear mirror-periodic coordinates, periods (142,80), and two-coset averaging. All independent cells use world origin phase (0,0). No original-game pixels. Summer grass: unmirrored periodic bilinear source sampling. Per source axis, overlap=(size-1)/4 and span=3*(size-1)/4. At world phase t in [0,period), x=t/period*span. For x\u003coverlap blend source(x+span) toward source(x) with cubic smoothstep(x/overlap); otherwise source(x). Apply separable windows on both axes, periods142,80. Round wrapped world phases to1e-9 before source lookup. Average RGB of f(x,y),f(x+71,y+40), then round half-up once. This is invariant under all six neighbor translations without reflected source marks. Non-grass materials, unseen and winter retain the existing sampler.",
  "tool": "Go tools/art-review -connected",
  "trench_profile": {
    "blind_spur_length_world_px": 14,
    "cap_beyond_center_world_px": 14,
    "chamber_floor_size_world_px": [
      10,
      9
    ],
    "courses": "Each port runs straight 16 world px inward, then via a point 13 world px from center with a 2-world-pixel transverse offset to center. A single port with no explicit blind spurs extends 14 world px beyond center and ends in a round cap; explicit blind spurs supersede that implicit tail. Blind spurs run center to unit-neighbor*14 with round caps. A dugout uses an independent narrow neck from center to unit-neighbor*15 with floor width min(0.6*width,3.5), no width wear, and a separate rounded 10x9 floor chamber (corner radius 2), aligned with its direction. The neck is excluded from the full-width main course. Ring is a new 36x26 rounded rectangle centerline with radius 7, sampled 16 segments per quarter; center remains open.",
    "dugout_neck_max_width_world_px": 3.5,
    "dugout_neck_width_fraction": 0.6,
    "dugout_offset_world_px": 15,
    "guards": "The first 8 world px from every polygon edge have fixed width/bank and no wear. Straight continuation to 16 px keeps angular courses and their radius outside that guard. Width wear is 0.18*E*sin(3A+B). Bank fringe is E*(0.25*sin(2B-A)+0.8*clamp((L-110)/100,-0.6,0.8)), where L=0.2126R+0.7152G+0.0722B of the sampled earth material; its clods roughen only the interior bank silhouette. E=S((edge_distance-8)/8), A=2pi(x/142+y/80), B=2pi(x/142-y/80). Texture, wood phase and shading repeat on the runtime lattice; actual exported PNG joins use existing overscan/Lanczos/final ownership and ordinary decoded blits.",
    "interior_straight_world_px": 16,
    "method": "Trench only: new dark earth floor, shaded new earth banks and new timber revetment/braces. Geometry uses numeric runtime ports only; no original pixels, masks or outlines. Candidate appearance requires visual review.",
    "port_guard_world_px": 8,
    "revetment_width_world_px": 1.1,
    "ring_centerline_size_world_px": [
      36,
      26
    ],
    "ring_corner_radius_world_px": 7,
    "shading": "Let N be the unit vector from the nearest main-course/neck point to the sample, or the chamber SDF gradient (central differences at +/-0.01 world px) for a chamber-owned sample; N=(0,0) at length \u003c=1e-9. D=round(dot(N,(0.6,0.8))*1e9)/1e9. Wall=S((core_distance+2.25)/2.25). Floor samples trench at 0.72*(1-0.6*Wall*(0.5+0.5*D)) brightness, producing a consistent southeast inner-wall shadow. Banks sample earth at (0.94+0.1*sin(A+0.4)*cos(B))*(1-0.15*D) brightness. Timber is source*1.08 brightness; revetment is a 1.1-world-pixel band centered 0.1 px inside the floor edge. Braces use clamp(0.5+(sin(3A+2B)-0.97)/0.06,0,1) and reach 1.2 world px from the floor edge. RGB rounds to nearest byte and clamps to 255. Reciprocal straight guards share nearest-course world normals, textures and phases. Core remains opaque; only the exterior 0.25-world-pixel analytic AA ramp is translucent. No baked grass. Interior timber breakup: multiply the revetment by 1-E+E*S((sin(12A+4B+0.7sin(3A-2B))+0.15)/0.7), creating separate planks with dark gaps. Add interior braces with E²*ramp(sin(6A+2B)-0.92,0.08)*ramp(1.4-abs(core_distance),AA). The squared fade preserves readable directional wall shading through the guard transition. Guard E=0 retains the original continuous reciprocal revetment and original braces.",
    "traverse_offset_world_px": 2
  },
